WEBVTT

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.480
Hey, I'll give you a massage.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.600
No, that's all right.

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:18.130
You know, I've had to fight the urge to do something for you every time I saw you looking exhausted and tired.

00:02:18.130 --> 00:02:19.110
Come on.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.180
I guess I was just anxious about your back.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:34.290
So you knew about my back?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:35.210
Yeah.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.880
Why didn't you say anything?

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:43.260
Coach Asaki told us not to say
anything until the meet was over.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.580
That woman.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:48.400
Does it hurt here?

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.270
Since when?

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:53.650
About a year or two after the old man died.

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:57.280
Looking back on it now, I can see he how careful he was.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.530
I'd want to jump from a high place,
and he'd always tell me to wait just a little longer.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:08.790
He was probably considering the physical stress and was waiting for your body to develop.

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:15.920
Hey. You think that's the reason the old man only taught me the basics?

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:17.950
I'd guess so.

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:23.680
Diving techniques only get riskier the more difficult they are.
The chance of failure increases too.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:26.960
And failing could be damaging to your body.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.060
Although, I suppose the lack of saving
technique instruction is a sign of his times.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.190
But Okitsu Shiraha was probably thinking about the long-term for your training.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.190
For what purpose?

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:42.700
Don't ask me that, dummy.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.200
Didn't you figure out how your grandpa felt at today's meet?

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.460
Anyway, you'll probably want to see a doctor.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.090
We'll figure out a plan after that.

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:10.290
The Japan Swimming Federation just announced the final roster for the Beijing camp.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:12.850
What is it?

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:14.630
I'm going home.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:15.720
What?

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.730
There's no way I was chosen.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:21.250
I'm aware enough to know that.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:23.690
Hold on.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:28.870
Don't you want to know which of your teammates,
who have been practicing up until now, were chosen?

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.370
Knowing that'll only piss me off.

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.790
Let's leave him be for a while.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:42.260
Back to the topic at hand.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:43.860
It's time to announce who was selected.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.540
The Japanese Swimming Federation selection committee

00:04:47.540 --> 00:04:51.890
has decided to send three male divers and three female divers to Beijing, just as they announced.

00:04:51.890 --> 00:04:54.770
The first male diver is Fujitani Youichi.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:57.270
Congratulations.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.530
You were a unanimous decision for the committee.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:02.780
Thank you.

00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:09.030
The second member is Matsuno from Tokushima,
who finished second on platform and third on springboard.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:14.290
The third member should've been Tsuji, but China's Coach Sun opposed.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:20.620
He was actually at the competition, and after watching the meet—

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.880
Just tell us who the third is already.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:24.890
It's you.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:25.550
What?

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:28.190
Coach Sun nominated you.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:29.680
However...

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.660
we declined the opportunity.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:33.680
What?!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:40.190
Even before receiving the JSF's offer, Coach Asaki,
Coach Ooshima, and I have had numerous conversations

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.350
and concluded that you wouldn't be able to do it right now.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:48.910
And so they picked a new candidate.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.990
And that candidate is you, Sakai.

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.340
What do you mean?

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.090
Coach Sun chose Okitsu, didn't he?

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:07.240
So why am I the one going?

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:14.970
Yes, it's true that Coach Sun was moved by Okitsu's boldness.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:16.170
However...

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:18.830
It's your back.

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.420
You understand, don't you?

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:22.880
The training camp is going to be too dangerous.

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:26.810
We thought it'd be best if you concentrated on recovering.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:28.710
Back?

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:30.620
Is your back hurt?

00:06:36.930 --> 00:06:39.000
I don't want this.

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.380
I don't want to go in Okitsu's place!

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.710
If I'm going to go, I'd rather it be when I'm better.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.950
I don't want to go unless I was chosen to.

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:49.160
Stop being naive.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:54.510
If you really think you're not any good,
then go to Beijing and learn everything you can.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:57.020
Anyway, this isn't how I want it!

00:06:57.020 --> 00:06:57.890
Tomo!

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:03.640
He can't use his teammate as a stepping stone.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:07.080
I hope that doesn't cost him.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.530
Sakai Tomoki will definitely go.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:17.800
Could you allow me some time to talk to Okitsu alone?

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:18.940
Of course.

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:25.410
Thanks for coming.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:27.550
I'm sorry things didn't work out for you.

00:07:27.550 --> 00:07:29.580
It's a competitive world, after all.

00:07:30.390 --> 00:07:35.930
But sometimes I think about team sports like
volleyball with a team of six and baseball with nine.

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:40.140
It must be nice to fight and win together as a team.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.810
<i>Fight together.</i>

00:07:45.350 --> 00:07:47.440
<i>And win together.</i>

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:49.720
<i>Yes.</i>

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:51.210
<i>That is nice.</i>

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.820
Why don't you want to go?

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.080
I wasn't even chosen...

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.560
I'm not even good enough...

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.100
You like diving, don't you?

00:08:04.530 --> 00:08:09.230
I got so absorbed with diving that I didn't notice how awkward it became with my friends,

00:08:09.230 --> 00:08:11.910
and my younger brother stole my girlfriend,

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:16.110
but it's still important to me.

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:19.770
You have something that others don't.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:23.140
Your diamond eyes.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:31.220
But you know, nobody will think you're cool if you let
your pride get in the way of using it to its full potential.

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.530
Well, I know I'm not cool anyway.

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:37.660
Hey, I'll start calling you Matsuno from Tokushima.

00:08:38.660 --> 00:08:40.220
Don't...

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:42.570
Then stop with the self-pity.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.040
You were chosen.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:47.240
You weren't the only one who could've replaced Okitsu.

00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:49.660
It could've been Pinky or Jirou!

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:52.300
But they chose you!

00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:56.680
If you throw away this chance,
you've got no right to call yourself a diver!

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.930
If you're going to turn this down,
then don't bother competing at all!

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:04.630
Just jump into a pond on your way home or something.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:07.550
I don't want to do that.

00:09:07.550 --> 00:09:09.070
The heck is that?

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:17.350
Then...

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:20.950
Let's surprise everyone in Beijing.

00:09:21.570 --> 00:09:22.560
You and me.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.710
What did you want to talk to me about?

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.160
Just say it already.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:10.790
We should've talked to you first before making any decision.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.560
I know that.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:20.020
But even if we talked to you, you would've been reckless enough to do whatever you had to in order to go.

00:10:20.020 --> 00:10:23.520
I couldn't let you do something so suicidal.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:30.940
I couldn't let you risk your entire career as a diver over one little trip to Beijing.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:37.320
But I thought this little trip to Beijing
was the only shortcut to the Olympics.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:39.930
Next year's Olympics aren't the only one.

00:10:39.930 --> 00:10:42.450
It'll come around again in five and nine years.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:46.060
Which means that there's no hope for next year for me?

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:48.080
Is my back really that bad?

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:51.760
We won't know unless a specialist takes a look.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:57.840
However bad the injury might be,
I think it's difficult for a back injury to completely recover.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.890
You'll just have to figure out how
you'll want to work around the injury.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.100
Work around?

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:08.950
It means we'll use every trick in the book to keep you practicing without aggravating your injury.

00:11:08.950 --> 00:11:10.730
You won't be able to learn any new dives.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:17.120
Instead, master the saving technique to lessen the stress on your back.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:19.820
But even then, the pain will likely linger.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:23.300
The question is if you'll be able to endure it.

00:11:23.300 --> 00:11:25.240
Why say that now?!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.060
What?

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.950
You knew about my back,

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:34.500
but you told Coach Fujitani and Coach Ooshima not to say anything until after the competition.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.250
You're right, that's not what a coach should've done.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:43.640
But I wanted you to experience the thrill of the crowd, even if it was only once.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:48.640
Is that why you let me dive the way I wanted to?

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:54.650
And when you were free to do your own diving style,
you grabbed Coach Sun's attention.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.190
Tell me.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:02.910
That day, were you able to experience that momentary thrill?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.680
You...

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.060
You need something?

00:12:32.560 --> 00:12:34.920
Yeah, um...

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:37.110
Is Tomoki here?

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.160
Tomo?

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:48.120
Okitsu?!

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.290
Yo.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.840
Is your back okay?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:56.380
It's fine as long as I don't exert myself.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:13:00.130
So were you in pain every time you dove this whole time?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:02.980
Forget about that for now.

00:13:05.340 --> 00:13:07.610
Go to Beijing.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:09.580
Youichi told me the same thing.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:11.320
Don't lose out on this chance.

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:15.380
Remember how you were telling me that you wanted to surpass your limits with diving?

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:17.270
Yeah, you're right.

00:13:17.610 --> 00:13:22.680
Youichi also told me that if I turned this down, something terrible would happen.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:23.530
Huh?

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:27.780
If the next candidate turns out to be Pinky...

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.340
You mean the guy with the pink swimsuit?

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:31.070
Yeah.

00:13:31.070 --> 00:13:35.000
He said he's the embarrassment of Japan that we couldn't let out into the world.

00:13:36.590 --> 00:13:39.040
Yeah, but Fujitani's suit's...

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.240
Lemon yellow.

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:43.090
Maybe that's why he hates him.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.580
They overlap too much.

00:13:49.880 --> 00:13:55.510
In the qualifiers, I was really happy in the beginning when I got fourth for the very first time.

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:59.080
But Youichi ran away with first place,

00:13:59.080 --> 00:14:01.460
and the crowd was watching you.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:04.070
I did my best,

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:06.720
but I felt like I just didn't have enough.

00:14:07.340 --> 00:14:12.310
The night after the competition,
my frustration kept me from sleeping.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.700
You've changed.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.050
Have I?

00:14:17.050 --> 00:14:18.340
Yeah.

00:14:18.340 --> 00:14:21.890
You're completely different from when I first met you.

00:14:21.890 --> 00:14:24.640
Especially during the qualifiers.

00:14:24.640 --> 00:14:26.430
Did something happen?

00:14:26.430 --> 00:14:27.240
Huh?

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:30.610
Well, I guess heartbreak?

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:31.430
What?

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.030
You met my younger brother earlier when you came to my house, right?

00:14:37.030 --> 00:14:39.290
Oh, so that was your younger brother?

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:41.070
He took her from me.

00:14:42.360 --> 00:14:45.590
While I was too busy being absorbed with diving,

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:50.400
my younger brother was kissing my girlfriend who I hadn't even held hands with.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:54.120
Did you like the girl?

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:59.730
I don't know, but it's like I started to like her after all this had happened.

00:15:00.380 --> 00:15:01.500
Is that weird?

00:15:03.860 --> 00:15:07.670
No, it's so pure, I'm almost jealous.

00:15:09.830 --> 00:15:15.760
Listen, we don't want you being outdone in Beijing,
so we're going to make sure you perfect the three-and-a-half.

00:15:15.760 --> 00:15:16.600
Okay!

00:15:17.250 --> 00:15:19.560
If you improve your precision,

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:24.010
you'll be sure to catch Coach Sun's attention,
which will give you a chance to aim even higher.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:24.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:15:26.500 --> 00:15:29.300
It's just like you said.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:30.190
Huh?

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:34.450
You said that Sakai Tomoki will definitely go.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.380
Yes, that's right.

00:15:37.380 --> 00:15:40.040
He's stronger than he looks.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.860
<i>Is he weaker than he looks?</i>

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:50.820
So Ryou quit?

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:52.250
Seems like it.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:53.800
I can't believe it.

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.660
Are you sad?

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:59.350
I wouldn't say that.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.860
I'm more worried about myself.

00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:01.690
Huh?

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:07.550
What do you mean by that?

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:10.780
Because I'll need to fight on my own now.

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:20.000
Yo.

00:16:23.380 --> 00:16:27.040
You watching your calories like Youichi?

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.590
Something like that.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:31.840
Come on, call it your last ice cream bar.

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.340
Okay.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:40.420
I'm rooting for you, Reiji.

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:44.140
I mean, I'll try my best, but I don't know.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:49.980
Although, I can't really say I ever
worked very hard until just recently.

00:16:50.470 --> 00:16:55.990
It used to be that I wouldn't even need to
put much effort into beating you or Tomo.

00:16:56.400 --> 00:17:02.000
I was always the best of the three of us
without having to work hard at practice.

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:06.790
But after that woman coach showed up,
everything completely changed.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:11.260
I'm sure this is what the real ranking should be, though.

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.380
You thought of all this after just one competition result?

00:17:16.330 --> 00:17:18.510
You already figured it out yourself, right?

00:17:19.300 --> 00:17:23.100
I was so frustrated that only Tomo was being taught the three-and-a-half.

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:26.720
After that, I did my individual training without skipping anything.

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:29.370
But I couldn't win.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:32.030
It's the same with me.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:36.020
I thought that I couldn't ever beat him anymore.

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.360
Or you for that matter.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.410
Me?

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:39.960
Yeah.

00:17:39.960 --> 00:17:44.410
That's why I started to think it was stupid
to work hard on something for no results.

00:17:45.260 --> 00:17:46.940
So that's how it is.

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.330
I should get going.

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:57.620
Tell Tomo good luck for me!

00:18:04.340 --> 00:18:05.680
You're back.

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:07.560
We're having sukiyaki tonight!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.690
Isn't that great?

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:09.910
Look at this.

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.320
This is top quality beef.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:20.820
I hear that the Kanto and Kansai
regions make sukiyaki differently.

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:22.200
Did you know that?

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.510
No.

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:26.330
Kanto style is seasoning it with sukiyaki stock.

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:31.340
Kansai style is gradually adding flavor
depending on the amount of ingredients.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.280
Today we'll be doing it Kanto style.

00:18:34.280 --> 00:18:36.470
I don't care which it is as long as I can eat.

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.650
What's wrong with you?

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.840
These kinds of things are important.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.480
It's unnatural.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:50.660
All right, break the egg, mix it up, and eat some meat.

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.110
What's unnatural?

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:54.220
The sukiyaki.

00:18:54.220 --> 00:19:00.070
I don't know if you're trying to be considerate or something, but it's just making it seem more unnatural.

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:02.520
What's wrong with sukiyaki?

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:05.310
I even splurged and got the good meat.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:08.000
The sukiyaki isn't the issue.

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:09.800
Okay, okay.

00:19:09.800 --> 00:19:13.570
I know I'm not the type of guy who can casually do something thoughtful.

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:15.670
I can't say anything helpful.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.510
I'm just a loser who could only think of sukiyaki.

00:19:19.210 --> 00:19:20.270
Just say it.

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:26.730
So, what are you going to do now?

00:19:26.730 --> 00:19:27.960
About what?

00:19:27.960 --> 00:19:31.370
What do you mean what, idiot? I'm talking about diving.

00:19:31.370 --> 00:19:33.120
You're asking me that?

00:19:33.120 --> 00:19:34.900
I wasn't planning to.

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.120
But you told me to say it.

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:42.150
Although, it's a little tactless to
bring up diving at the family table.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:45.910
Hold on, do you see a family here? Is that what we are?

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:49.360
Come on, I've always wanted one.

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:53.170
It's my dream to have a family conversation with my son around the dinner table.

00:19:55.140 --> 00:19:58.800
You know, I'm glad I'm not your son.

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:03.920
Hey.

00:20:03.920 --> 00:20:05.680
Just make sure you see a doctor.

00:20:07.900 --> 00:20:10.680
Part of me feels like it's not necessary anymore.

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:12.690
What do you mean by that?

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:39.340
Is this where we were supposed to meet?

00:20:39.860 --> 00:20:42.630
I should've come here with Youichi...

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:44.740
Youichi!

00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:45.470
Hey.

00:20:45.860 --> 00:20:48.220
This is where we were supposed to meet, right?

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:49.800
Probably.

00:20:49.800 --> 00:20:53.350
I wasn't sure since nobody else had shown up.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:54.230
I'm here.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:55.230
Huh?

00:20:57.700 --> 00:20:59.230
Um...

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:02.260
It's Matsuno from Tokushima.

00:21:02.260 --> 00:21:03.530
Right.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:17.540
Maybe I didn't need to say love.
